HISTORY closest to the bottom of the detector that is closest to the            HISTORY bottom of the slit (i.e. also closest to the bottom of the              HISTORY detector).  Moving up the detector, the FITS array is filled in         HISTORY with subsequent extraction apertures.  If no orders have been           HISTORY deselected in the extraction process, the contents of the ith           HISTORY aperture in order j can be found as follows:                            HISTORY lambda=array[*,0,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)],                         HISTORY flux=array[*,1,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)],                           HISTORY uncertainty=array[*,2,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)],                    HISTORY flag=array[*,3,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)].                           HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY The spectra in the file(s) spectra0113.fits, spectra0114.fits,          HISTORY spectra0115.fits, spectra0116.fits, spectra0117.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0118.fits, spectra0119.fits, spectra0120.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0121.fits, spectra0122.fits, spectra0123.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0124.fits, spectra0125.fits, spectra0126.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0127.fits, spectra0128.fits, spectra0129.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0130.fits, spectra0131.fits, spectra0132.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0133.fits, spectra0134.fits, spectra0135.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0136.fits, spectra0241.fits, spectra0242.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0243.fits, spectra0244.fits, spectra0245.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0246.fits, spectra0247.fits, spectra0248.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0249.fits, spectra0250.fits were combined using a robust         HISTORY weighted mean with a sigma threshold of 8.  Aperture 1                  HISTORY modifications: The scale factors were determined using order 4          